          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Once beyond the realm of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+spaces"} normed vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
            diverge. This is particularly evident if one considers the slightly stronger notion of
            %strong continuous differentiability
            wherein the assignment of the derivative must also be continuous.
          %p
            One can make a reasonable start by saying that for a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊇
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon E \supseteq U \to F
            to be continuously differentiable then it must at least satisfy the notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%A2teaux+differentiability"} Gâteaux differentiability
            = succeed ")." do
              %em Gâteaux–Lévy differentiability
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D f \colon U \to \mathcal{L}(E,F)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(E,F)
            and thus one can come up with a variety of meanings for the phrase “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D f
            is continuous”.
          %h2#finite_dimensions Finite Dimensions
          %p Let us remind ourselves of the situation in finite dimensions.
          #ctsd.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi m
                      %mo ⊇
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^m \supseteq U \to \mathbb{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is open, is said to be
              = succeed "," do
                %strong continuously differentiable
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D f \colon U \to \mathcal{L}(\mathbb{R}^m, \mathbb{R}^n)
              with the property that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in \mathbb{R}^m
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi t
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                        %mi D
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi h
                      %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lim_{t \to 0} \frac{f(x + t h) - f(x) - t D f(x)h}{t} = 0
          %p
            Note that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in \mathbb{R}^n
            there is an open interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\epsilon,\epsilon)
            with the property that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in (-\epsilon,\epsilon)
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi t
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + t h \in U
            and so the limit makes sense.
          %h2#infinite_dimensions Infinite Dimensions
          %p
            In infinite dimensions the difficulty with extending the standard definition is that of the topology on continuous linear maps. This becomes more evident with higher derivatives. Thus the definition depends on such a choice. In addition, one needn’t use a topology but can make sense of the definition with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+structure"} convergence structure
            on the space of linear maps.
          #ctsdinf.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+topological+vector+spaces"} locally convex topological vector spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq E
              be an open set. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(E,F)
              be the space of continuous linear maps from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+structure"} convergence structure
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(E,F)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon U \to F
              is said to be
              %strong
                differentiable of class
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mi Λ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1_\Lambda
              if there exists a continuous mapping
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi Λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D f \colon U \to \mathcal{L}_\Lambda(E,F)
              %strong derivative
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,h \in U \times E
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi t
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mi D
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lim_{t \to 0} \frac{f(x + t h) - f(x)}{t} = D f(x) h
            %p
              We define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mi Λ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1_\Lambda(X,F)
              to be the set of functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to F
              which are of class
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mi Λ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1_\Lambda
          %h2#convergence_structures Convergence Structures
          %p
            There are a variety of convergence structures and topologies on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(E,F)
            that can be used. Some of them with particular properties are gathered in the list below. For these, the notation is condensed slightly as indicated.
          %p
            In the following, given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-norms"} semi-norms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            we define a semi-norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ,
                      %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_{\beta,\alpha}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(E,F)
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ,
                      %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi sup
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho_{\beta,\alpha}(u) \coloneqq \sup \{\beta(u h) | \alpha(h) \le 1\}
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mi Θ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1_\Theta
                \: the translation-invariant convergence structure with filters:
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \to 0
                if there is a semi-norm
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                such that for each semi-norm
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \gt 0
                there is some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℱ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \in \mathcal{F}
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi sup
                          %mrow
                            %mi u
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi Q
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mrow
                            %mi β
                            %mo ,
                            %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi ϵ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sup_{u \in Q} \rho_{\beta,\alpha}(u) \le \epsilon
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1_\Delta
                \: (Marinescu’s convergence structure) the colimit in the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+vector+spaces"} convergence vector spaces
                of the following family of spaces. Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                denote the family of mappings from the set of continuous semi-norms on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                to that on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in \Phi
                define:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi u
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext for all
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{L}_\phi(E,F) \coloneqq \{ u \in \mathcal{L}(E,F) | \rho_{\beta,\phi(\beta)} \lt \infty\; \text{for all}\; \beta\}
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1_\Pi
                \: the compatible convergence structure with filters:
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \to 0
                if for each semi-norm
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                there is a semi-norm
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                such that for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \gt 0
                there is some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℱ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \in \mathcal{F}
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi sup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mrow
                            %mi β
                            %mo ,
                            %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi u
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi ϵ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sup\{\rho_{\beta,\alpha}(u) | u \in Q\} \le \epsilon
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mi b
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^1_{q b}
                \: the
                %em quasi-bounded
                convergence structure. This has filters:
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \to 0
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℬ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{B}^n) \to 0
                for every quasi-bounded filter
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %p
                Recall that a filter
